{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838434Z","id":"66edd5a0bd881986659a2ea2d5b4707358db0bb7b8afc03b86035bbdf34e3aa1","body":{"detail":"Commit 6598f558 (version restore audit fields) also added `\"db_read_grants\"` to fields_class as Class::Safe. At that commit no code writes a db_read_grants field into an artifact.update record: the field belongs to the cross-app read grant work (migration 24, crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs), still uncommitted when 6598f558 landed. Whether grant contents (artifact IDs of granted readers) are Safe under every redaction option is a decision for that work, and toolpath/tests.rs (the export test around line 1600 that asserts no unclassified fields) does not exercise it. Whoever lands the grant store should test this classification with a recorded grant change, or move the line into that commit's scope.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":313},"content_hash":"655c2658889e9a0dcd807bc7f24dc2468211c3b80066f0d33453185f050cd26e"},"summary":"db_read_grants is classified Safe in artifact.update fields with no code that emits it and no test in the commit that added it","tags":["redaction","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838627Z","id":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs:225 classifies version.publish `restored_from` as Safe, which is right for a version number. The test that walks every recorded audit row and asserts redact::unclassified is empty (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs, around line 1620) builds its history without Store::restore_version, and the restore tests in crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs check the stored body, not its redaction. Adding a restore to that fixture would pin the class.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1590},"end":{"line":1625},"content_hash":"f4df98f81f2f3085daeb071c708e2b3ccf96a632b353ab3a48471dcb75ea8503"},"summary":"The every-kind export test records no restore, so nothing fails if restored_from loses its redaction class","tags":["tests","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013567Z","id":"fe35d36ae19533e5a1219cc57c7536f6a994f5dbeb68cb24cec89d9b2a8ec25e","body":{"detail":"grant_record writes artifact.update with fields.db_read_grants = {\"grant\"|\"revoke\": <source artifact ID>} and artifact2_id = source. An artifact ID is Safe under every Redaction option (no_text, no_names, no_paths), so the class is right. What is missing is a recorded grant and revoke in the fixture of the every-kind export test (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs around 1590-1625), so a renamed field or a lost class fails a test.","kind":"comment","references":"66edd5a0bd881986659a2ea2d5b4707358db0bb7b8afc03b86035bbdf34e3aa1","summary":"The emitter now exists (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:40-50, commit 34851af8); the classification is still untested by the export test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013584Z","id":"beff378b4015d75b551944a057c4d8293194e9dbe3c20342ed7359e66f6151e9","body":{"detail":"The same fixture gap leaves fields.db_read_grants (record 66edd5a0) unexercised. One change covers both: call Store::restore_version and Store::grant_read / Store::revoke_read in the fixture before the audit rows are read, so redact::unclassified and assert_valid see version.publish restored_from and artifact.update fields.db_read_grants.","kind":"comment","references":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","summary":"Add the restore and a grant/revoke to this fixture together","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695598Z","id":"258a820ab944ed55d2d28b2b8c53903001cd98a37b4c6d958bf146b9f54f5844","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e1d562f","summary":"every_recorded_kind_is_classified_and_renders_conformant (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs) now records a grant and a revoke, which emit fields.db_read_grants. Evidence: with db_read_grants removed from fields_class the test fails with `artifact.update: unclassified [\"fields/db_read_grants\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"66edd5a0bd881986659a2ea2d5b4707358db0bb7b8afc03b86035bbdf34e3aa1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695752Z","id":"d251b4a4a139636753240bdde43cf423755c526b0dacb79dec3a06143295fc4a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e1d562f","summary":"The every-kind export fixture now publishes a second version and restores version 1 (restored_from), and makes and revokes a read grant, asserting both are among the live events. Evidence: with restored_from removed from body_class the test fails with `version.publish: unclassified [\"restored_from\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
